        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "We are given the equation:\n\n\\[\n1 + A = \\frac{B}{C}\n\\]\n\nWith:\n- \\( A = 10.957 \\)\n- \\( B = 5.65 \\)\n\n### Step-by-step solution:\n\n1. Plug in the values:\n\n\\[\n1 + 10.957 = \\frac{5.65}{C}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n11.957 = \\frac{5.65}{C}\n\\]\n\n2. Solve for \\( C \\):\n\n\\[\nC = \\frac{5.65}{11.957}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nC \\approx 0.4725\n\\]\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n\\[\nC \\approx \\boxed{0.4725}\n\\]\n\nWould you like help verifying this in a calculator or using it in another formula?"
          ]
        },
